{% tool-context
   title="System Cost Estimator"
   question="What will this architecture cost at its real operating envelope?"
   definition="A useful system cost estimate starts with workload and reliability requirements, derives the resources they need, then applies explicit unit-price assumptions. The number is only meaningful when its formulas and uncertainty remain visible."
   inputs="Set traffic, measured instance capacity, storage growth, replication, egress, utilization, and failure reserve. Then edit every illustrative price, regional factor, commitment assumption, and uncertainty range."
   outcome="See the scenario-ready fleet, durable data footprint, transfer volume, monthly cost range, exact cost drivers, and the reliability trade-off behind each optimization."
   experiment="Start with planned demand, then inject a traffic spike, replication growth, egress shock, and zone failure. Identify which challenge changes architecture, which changes only the bill, and where the current fleet loses reserve." /%}

